Files for test 793 (crypto): a P-256 key made by openssl (test only, public), its
public key, and openssl's DER signature (hex) of msg.txt, which ktm verifies.
For test 845 (RSA keys): a 2048-bit RSA key made by openssl (test only, public),
its public key, openssl's PKCS#1 v1.5 signatures of msg.txt with SHA-256/384/512
(hex), and an Ed25519 key, a kind crypto.Key doesn't take.
For test 846 (keys from JWK parts): rsa-n.hex, the modulus of rsa-pub.pem (its
exponent is 65537), and ec-x.hex, ec-y.hex, the point of pub.pem, as openssl
prints them.
For test 860 (Ed25519): ed-key.pem and ed-pub.pem (openssl), ed-msg.hex (1023
random bytes) and ed-sig.hex (openssl's signature of them); ed-key-truncated.pem
and ed-key-trailing.pem must be refused. (ed25519-key.pem reads since 0.23.0, so
test 845's "a kind of key Key doesn't take" is k256-key.pem, a secp256k1
key, now.)
For test 861 (P-384, P-521): p384-key.pem, p521-key.pem and their public PEMs
(openssl), their points (p384-x.hex ...), and openssl's signatures of msg.txt
(SHA-384 for P-384, SHA-512 for P-521) as DER and as raw r||s.
